{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>For there is no divination in Jacob.</b> For they are worthy of blessing — there are among them no diviners and soothsayers." "<b>As at this time it shall be said of Jacob, etc.</b> There will yet be a time like this time, when their belovedness will be revealed before the eyes of all — that they sit before Him and learn Torah from His mouth, and their discourse is before the ministering angels, and they ask them: <b>What has El wrought?</b> And this is what is said (Isaiah 30): ״וְהָיוּ עֵינֶיךָ רֹאוֹת אֶת מוֹרֶיךָ״. Another interpretation — <b>it shall be said of Jacob</b> is not future tense but present tense: they have no need to divine or divine by soothsaying, for at every time that something needs to be said to Jacob and to Israel — what the Holy One, blessed be He, has done and what His decrees are on high — they do not divine and consult soothsayers, but it is said to them through the mouth of their prophets what the decree of the Omnipresent is, or the Urim and Tummim declare it to them (Tanchuma); and Onkelos did not render thus."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:31.536329424Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}